post.description:
This endpoint allows adding additional product options like engraving, customizations or additional services to an existing product in the cart.
<br /><br />
Below you'll find a sample request for adding two product options (engraving and font type) to a cart with id C1234, to order line with LineItemId "a43707ab-1ebf-4114-8c48-eb0374932a4c", which in this case is a diamond ring.
<br />
The product options "P3" and "P5" should be valid SKUs for products in Omnium, with product type set to <code>ProductOption</code>.
<br />
The price for the product option will set from A: a specific price set in the parameter price, as displayed below. B: The price specified for the product option. C: The price specified for the product matching the sku.
            
    POST /api/carts/AddProductOptionsItemToCart
    {
        {
            "cartId": "C1234", // The unique identifier of the cart
            "parentLineItemId": "a43707ab-1ebf-4114-8c48-eb0374932a4c", // The ID of the existing order line to which product options are added
            "productOptions": [
                {
                    "skuId": "P3", // SKU ID of the product option
                    "title": "Font type", // Name of the product option
                    "value": "Big and bold" // The selected option value
                    "price": 199 // Optional: If you do not et the price in the request, the price will be fetched from the product in Omnium
                },
                {
                    "skuId": "P5",
                    "title": "Engraving",
                    "value": "omnium4ever"
                },
                {
                    "skuId": "P8" // It would often be sufficient to only use the skuId. The price and values would then fall back to the product option or the store product
                }
            ]
        }
    }
            
            
This would add three additional order lines to the cart, which would result in a diamond ring engraved with "omnium4ever" with font type "Big and bold", and also the option "P8" which in this case is an ultra nice gift box 💍
<br />

Sample request for a delta query:

    POST /api/inventory/search
    {
       "LastModified": "2019-11-21T17:32:28Z"
    }
            
Sample request for inventory for a specific market

    POST /api/inventory/search
    {
       "MarketId:" "NOR"
    }        

Samples response if the number of inventory items exceeds 1000 (totalHits).
<br /> 
Notice that the 'scrollId' property has been populated as totalHits exceeds 1000, meaning that you should use the scroll endpoint to fetch remaining inventory items
            
    {
      "totalHits": 41244,
      "result": [
        {
            "sku": "102103",
            "warehouseCode": "40",
            "inventory": 33,
            "reservedInventory": 7,
            "location": "32D-A2"
        },
        {
          "sku": "102104",
          ...
        }
      ],
      "scrollId": "2f842421e06e4c60bb2c4f0d8b3ef60b"
    }
        

Please note that if the total amount is larger than 2000, the response will contain a Scroll ID which can be used with the Scroll endpoint to fetch all remaining items.

patch.description:
Sample request for patching order line with lineItemId "1". Updating color and placedPrice.
            
    PATCH /api/{orderId}/patchUpdateOrderLines
    {
        [
            {
                "lineItemId": "1",
                "color" : "blue",
                "placedPrice": 100
            }
        ]
    }

put.description:
Sample request:
            
    PUT /api/orders/EPIC000001/AddOrderLineProperties
    [
        {
            "lineItemId": "1",
            "properties": [
                {
                    "key": "color",
                    "value": "red"
                },
                {
                    "key": "size",
                    "value": "medium"
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "lineItemId": "2",
            "properties": [
                {
                    "key": "color",
                    "value": "blue"
                },
                {
                    "key": "size",
                    "value": "large"
                }
            ]
        }
    ]

post.description:
If you need to update status on a shipment and not the order, set the corresponding "shipmentId" on the "shipmentInfo" object. The shipmentInfo object also allows you to update shipment information, such as tracking link or shipping method.
<br />
If you do not wish to automatically run the workflow for the order or shipment, you can specify this using "skipRunWorkflow:true".
<br /><br />
Basic example on how you would update status to "InProgress" for an existing order:
            
     POST /api/orders/{orderId}/UpdateStatus
     {
         "status": "InProgress"
     }
            
Example on how you would set status for an existing shipment (with shipmentId "1") to "Completed" and run workflow for the shipment while also updating tracking url:
            
     POST /api/orders/{orderId}/UpdateStatus
     {
         "status": "Completed",
         "shipmentInfo": { 
              "shipmentId": "1",
              "trackingUrl" : "https://omnium.no/not-an-actual-tracking-link"
         }
     }

If no <i>shipmentId</i> is set, the first (and possible only) shipment is used. If a non-existing shipment ID is specific, a new shipment will be created. <br />
If you target an existing shipment, by specifying shipmentId, you could also update shipment tracking link/number and shippingMethodName.
If you create a new partial shipment and do not specify shipping information, shipping information will be copied from the previous existing shipment.<br />
Combination of deliveredQuantity and splitQuantity should not be used. SplitQuantity will then be ignored.
<br /><br /> 
Example on how you create a partial delivered shipment (with shipmentId "2" - this could be set to any string) containing order lines with lineItemId "4" and "6", to "Completed" and run workflow for the shipment:
            
     POST /api/orders/1234/OrderLinesUpdate
     {
         "status": "Completed",
         "lineItemUpdates": [
         {
             "lineItemId": "4",
             "deliveredQuantity": 4
         },
         {
             "lineItemId": "6",
             "deliveredQuantity": 6
         }
         ],
         "shipmentInfo": { 
             "shipmentId": "2",
             "shippingMethodName": "Bring"
         }
     }
            

 <br />
 Example on how you create a partial shipment without delivered items(using splitQuantity, with shipmentId "2" - this could be set to any string) containing order lines with lineItemId "4" and "6", to "InProgress" and run workflow for the shipment.
 If the new partial shipment should be sent from a different warehouse that original shipment, set shipmentInfo.warehouseCode:
            
     POST /api/orders/1234/OrderLinesUpdate
     {
         "status": "InProgress",
         "lineItemUpdates": [
         {
             "lineItemId": "4",
             "splitQuantity": 2
         },
         {
             "lineItemId": "6",
             "splitQuantity": 1
         }
         ],
         "shipmentInfo": { 
             "shipmentId": "2",
             "shippingMethodName": "Bring",
             "warehouseCode: "warehouse4"
         }
     }
            

 <br /> 
Example on how you would set status for an existing shipment (with shipmentId "1") to "Completed", while setting delivered quantity and cancelled quantity:
            
     POST /api/orders/1234/OrderLinesUpdate
     {
         "status": "Completed",
         "lineItemUpdates": [
         {
             "lineItemId": "4",
             "deliveredQuantity": 4
         },
         {
             "lineItemId": "5",
             "deliveredQuantity": 2,
             "canceledQuantity": 3
         },
         {
             "lineItemId": "6",
             "canceledQuantity": 6
         }
         ],
         "shipmentInfo": { 
             "shipmentId": "1"
         }
     }
